The residual is discharged. The key point is that a same-residue change \(\Delta=\Phi _1'-\Phi _1''\) has strictly excessive \(w_1\)-weight. Dividing the correction term \(Q''\Delta\) by \(\Phi _1'\) changes \(R,Q\), but only above the two consumed weight lines, so the prescribed read is unchanged.

